INSERT INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES
('overlord-shade', 'Overlord Shade', 'Pellcam Denbra (true name)', 'Deevil Overlord, leader of the Dragon Lords army', 'rifts', 'Deevil of Dyval (which kind of Deevil is not printed)', '13th Level Infernal Ley Line Walker (as printed)', 13, 'Miscreant', 'Effectively Immortal', '20 feet (6.1 m) at full size; shrinks at will to as little as 6 feet (1.8 m)', '2,000 pounds (900 kg)', '{"IQ":23,"ME":23,"MA":17,"PS":29,"PP":23,"PE":28,"PB":8,"Spd":37}', 290, 400, 500, 400, 160, 16, 17, '{"attacks":8,"initiative":4,"strike":7,"parry":7,"dodge":5,"pull":1,"roll":1}', 'Spd 37 on foot and 111 flying (75 mph/120 km); his Dragon Hide armor doubles the flying speed. Hit Points 290, S.D.C. 400 and A.R. 16 are the block''s S.D.C.-setting figures. Also +6 to save vs Horror Factor, +9 vs magic and +4 vs psionics. Supernatural P.S. 29. W.P. Blunt.', '[{"name":"Archaeology","pct":98},{"name":"Astronomy & Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Barter","pct":87},{"name":"Brewing","pct":94},{"name":"Chemistry","pct":98},{"name":"Chemistry: Analytical","pct":94},{"name":"Cryptography","pct":98},{"name":"Gemology","pct":94},{"name":"Holistic Medicine","pct":98},{"name":"Horsemanship: Exotic Animals","pct":98},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":89},{"name":"Interrogation","pct":98},{"name":"Literacy: American","pct":98},{"name":"Literacy: Demongogian","pct":98},{"name":"Literacy: Dragonese/Elven","pct":98},{"name":"Literacy: Dwarven","pct":98},{"name":"Literacy: Euro","pct":98},{"name":"Literacy: Greek","pct":98},{"name":"Literacy: Spanish","pct":98},{"name":"Literacy: Splugorth","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Demons & Monsters","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Faeries & Creatures of Magic","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Magic","pct":98},{"name":"Mathematics: Basic","pct":98},{"name":"Mathematics: Advanced","pct":98},{"name":"Mythology","pct":98},{"name":"Prowl","pct":94},{"name":"Public Speaking","pct":98},{"name":"Research","pct":98}]', 'Skills of note only. Archaeology, Holistic Medicine and Horsemanship: Exotic Animals are printed 98%/89% and Brewing 94%/98%; the first figure is kept. Printed as Language & Literacy at 98% for Dragonese, Dwarven, American, Greek, Splugorth, Demongogian, Euro and Spanish, kept here as literacies; Dragonese carries its catalog name, Dragonese/Elven, and American, Demongogian, Dwarven, Greek, Spanish and Splugorth have no catalog literacy row. Chemistry: Analytical is kept as printed; the catalog spells it with a dash. W.P. Blunt is printed without a percentage.', 'Supernatural P.S. and P.E. Bio-Regenerates 1D4x10 each melee round. Teleport 86% and Dimensional Teleport 76%. Nightvision 500 feet (152 m). Changes his size at will anywhere from 6 feet (1.8 m) up to his full 20 feet (6.1 m). Understands every language by magic. Draws 20 P.P.E. a melee from a ley line, 40 at a nexus. Impervious to electricity: lightning of any kind, ordinary or magical, does him no harm. Has every power of a Ley Line Walker. Vulnerabilities: weapons that do bonus damage to Deevils or to dragons and reptiles work on him, and Millennium Tree weapons do triple damage; his fixation on dragons leads him to chase every rumour almost blindly, and adult dragons who learn of his hobby are likely to become dangerous foes.', 'Ley Line Walker powers: Sense Ley Line and Magic Energy, Read Ley Lines, Ley Line Transmission, Ley Line Phasing, Ley Line Walking/Drifting, Ley Line Rejuvenation, Ley Line Observation Ball, Affinity with Rift & Ley Line Magic and Ley Line Force Field. Spells: every invocation of levels 1-4, plus Anti-Magic Cloud (140), Ballistic Fire (25), Blind (6), Calling (8), Call Lightning (5), Carpet of Adhesion (10), Close Rift (200+), Dimensional Portal (1000), Domination (10), Electric Arc (8), Energy Field (10), Escape (8), Havoc (70), Ice (15), Ley Line Defense (90), Ley Line Phantom (20), Ley Line Shutdown (3000), Ley Line Tendril Bolts (13), Lightning Arc (30), Magic Pigeon (20), Metamorphosis: Animal (25; reptiles only), Mystic Portal (20), Negate Magic (10), Plane Skip (33), Rift Teleportation (100), Rift to Limbo (80), Shadow Meld (10), Sleep (10), Soultwist (170), Summon Ley Line Storm (250), Summon Shadow Beast (140), Swallowing Rift (150), Teleport: Superior (600), The Slowness (1,300), Warrior Horde (1100) and Wind Rush (20). P.P.E. 400.', 'Astral Projection (8), Detect Psionics (6), Ectoplasm (6 or 12), Exorcism (10), Hypnotic Suggestion (6), Impervious to Fire (4), Impervious to Poison/Toxin (4), Mind Block (4), Mind Bolt (varies), Presence Sense (4), Psychosomatic Disease (30), Resist Fatigue (4), Resist Thirst (6), Telekinetic Lift (6), Telekinetic Push (4) and Telemechanics (10). I.S.P. 160; a Master Psionic. Impervious to Poison/Toxin is printed as Impervious to Poison.', NULL, NULL, 'Dragon Hide armor of 400 M.D.C. that doubles his flying speed and gives him a fire breath. A spiked club carved from dragon bone that has somehow taken on runes: it has the eight powers of a Rune Weapon, is of Diabolic alignment, its runes glow red with any dragon within 500 feet (152.4 m), and it can teleport back to its wielder three times a day from as far as 5 miles (8 km). He carries on his person at all times a scroll of Metamorphosis: Dragon, which he will neither use nor try to convert.', 'At least two treasure hoards in the manner of a dragon''s, each worth tens of millions.', 'Haughty: he holds nearly every other being his inferior, and his courtesy toward those he hopes to win over can vanish in an instant. Selfish and consumed by dragons, he wants to become one, or better, a god that dragons and mortals alike worship, so he gladly recruits and enslaves dragons and kills any who refuse him. The Minion War and the demons on Rifts Earth are chores he does to keep his masters content; most of his time goes to his own pursuits while underlings run the campaign.', 'At least three Shadow Lords in the Plane of Shadows, each of whom has promised him thousands of Shadow Beasts; what he gives them in return is unknown, though his troops whisper that he will share conquered land on Rifts Earth with them. Some dragons serve in his army, a few by choice because they are evil, the rest under blackmail and hating him for it. Lord Gray of the Shadow Forest in the Magic Zone has let him slip his troops quietly into North America.', 'Demons above all, and anyone who blocks or defies him; humans and D-Bees are toys and slaves to him. Several Deevil Regents resent his promotion to Overlord and have planted agents in his ranks to find his weak points, so an assassin may strike from inside his own army. Over the years he has also made foes of countless adult dragons, some of them in his own ranks.', 'The Deevil Lords sent him to Rifts Earth because he has built, almost alone, one of the largest and deadliest armies of the Minion War, swollen with Shadow Beasts and other Shadow Minions from his alliance with Shadow Lords. That army would be close to unstoppable with steady leadership, but he is fixated on dragons: he hoards their heads, bones, relics and armor, and roams abandoned lairs across the Megaverse, so he is often gone when his troops need him and keeps replacing lieutenants who die or defy him. Earth thrills him for its Dragon Kings, rumoured to know the secrets of the Shadow Dragons, for their lairs that may have outlasted the Coalition siege of Tolkeen, and for its many other dragons. His army, the Dragon Lords, flies a black flag trimmed in yellow bearing a golden dragon''s skull; it wins by sheer numbers, savagery and surprise troops rather than discipline, often teeters on collapse until he steps in, and would break into smaller bands if he fell. Its target is the American Midwest, Minnesota above all: his priorities run dragons first, then demons, then vampires, marching on the ruins of Tolkeen before all his Shadow Minions have arrived.', 'Rifts World Book 35: Megaverse in Flames p.158-161'),
('overlord-dai', 'Overlord Dai', 'D''hoty Odo (true name)', 'Self-proclaimed Deevil Overlord, the Little General, leader of the Tolkeen Avengers', 'rifts', 'Imp (Deevil of Dyval)', 'Sixth level; no O.C.C. is printed (as printed)', 6, 'Miscreant', 'Effectively Immortal', '3 feet (0.9 m)', '100 pounds (45 kg)', '{"IQ":14,"ME":16,"MA":26,"PS":15,"PP":12,"PE":20,"PB":14,"Spd":17}', 39, 30, 70, 70, NULL, 10, 10, '{"attacks":4,"strike":1,"parry":1,"dodge":3,"pull":2,"roll":4}', 'Spd 17 running and 29 flying (20 mph/32 km). Hit Points 39, S.D.C. 30 and A.R. 10 are the block''s S.D.C.-setting figures. Horror Factor 15 when he rides on Spike or fights beside him. Also +4 to save vs Horror Factor, +2 vs magic and +1 on Perception Rolls. Supernatural P.S. 15. W.P. Knife and W.P. Energy Rifle.', '[{"name":"Appraise Goods","pct":75},{"name":"Barter","pct":98},{"name":"Brewing","pct":81},{"name":"Climbing","pct":85},{"name":"Computer Operation","pct":95},{"name":"Concealment","pct":65},{"name":"Demolitions","pct":98},{"name":"Demolitions Disposal","pct":65},{"name":"Escape Artist","pct":75},{"name":"Find Contraband","pct":75},{"name":"Gambling (Standard)","pct":85},{"name":"Gambling (Dirty Tricks)","pct":75},{"name":"Gemology","pct":85},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":79},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":81},{"name":"Literacy: Demongogian","pct":90},{"name":"Lore: Demons & Monsters","pct":85},{"name":"Mathematics: Basic","pct":98},{"name":"Palming","pct":75},{"name":"Pick Locks","pct":71},{"name":"Prowl","pct":70},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":75}]', 'Skills of note only. Climbing is printed 85%/85% and the first figure is kept. Printed as Gambling, Gambling: Dirty Tricks and Lore: Demons and Monsters; those carry their catalog names. Literacy: Demongogian has no catalog row. Prowl is +10% while he hovers or flies.', 'Every ability an Imp has, among them flight, nightvision 90 feet (27.4 m), seeing the invisible, half damage from fire and cold, Bio-Regeneration of 1D6 a melee round and a magical knowledge of all languages. Vulnerabilities: drink and gambling are his weaknesses, exotic liquor (Phase World''s especially) most of all; he and Spike take first pick of all plunder and leave little for the rest, so his troops are less content than they were, and he has grown careless enough to leave openings for an assassin.', 'All level one spells plus Armor of Ithan (10), Aura of Power (4), Chameleon (6) and Invisibility: Simple (6). P.P.E. 70. He has the Sowki''s spell book and notes but finds study dull and drinks instead. His Dragon Rod can cast Circle of Flame, Fly, Magic Pigeon, Metamorphosis: Human and Metamorphosis: Animal, each up to three times in 24 hours.', 'None.', NULL, NULL, 'A magic cloak of 90 M.D.C. that teleports him up to 5 miles (8 km) three times a day once he wraps himself in it entirely; it is too long for him and trails behind as he walks. His treasure is the Dragon Rod, won in single combat: a Greater Rune Weapon shaped like an energy rifle with a dragon''s head, with the eight standard Rune Weapon powers, the spells listed under magic, three kinds of energy blast (each costs him one melee attack) and a blunt strike.', 'A trove of items gathered on Rifts Earth worth about 11 million credits.', 'Still a prankster and a reveller, but also a born leader with a fine grasp of strategy and tactics. Once he lived carefree from one party to the next; having tasted power he has shouldered an army and the ambitions that go with it. He can be petty and vengeful, yet his fellow misfits generally like him. For now he is brash, confident and sly, loves the feel of power and is coming to believe he truly is a great general who has earned the rank of Overlord.', 'Spike the Hangdog Daemonix, his best friend and most devoted follower; they are seldom apart, and Spike would die for him, though whether Dai would do the same is uncertain. Most of his Daemonix and the other outcasts are loyal and enjoy serving him while the fighting goes well. When the moment is right he means to approach his patron, the Deevil Lord Nickodeamis, hoping to be made an Overlord in earnest and sent more troops; Old Nick is likelier to send reinforcements and a word of praise, and a snub could send Dai rogue with his army, even into enmity with the Deevils.', 'The Demons of Hades first, then rival Deevil armies, the Coalition States, heroes and anyone in his path. Tolkeen resistance fighters may hold a grudge against him too.', 'An Imp who never earned his title. Once a battlefield courier who fled at the first sign of danger, he slept off a drinking bout in Dyval Prime through the demons'' first assault and then ran from world to world to escape the Deevil Lords'' anger. Reaching Rifts Earth amid the last siege of Tolkeen, he used his magic to rescue Spike, a Hangdog Daemonix pinned down by Coalition troops, then rode on Spike''s back directing him through the soldiers. Other Daemonix soon accepted him as leader, then refugees of Tolkeen''s fall (Brodkil, Black Faeries, Thornhead Demons, Witchlings and D-Bees), helped by Spike''s tall tales of his might. Years of carrying generals'' orders had taught him strategy without his knowing it, and he loves to command and to win. He gathers survivors of broken Deevil forces and stragglers of armies like Shade''s, who take his title on trust and stay for his clear leadership, and plans to drive the demons from North America and claim it for Dyval. His army, the Tolkeen Avengers, flies a dark green triangular standard bearing a red Imp in silhouette. A guerrilla force of supernatural beings, D-Bees, deserters and refugees, it raids Calgary, the Simvan and the Colorado Baronies for liquor and supplies from the Canadian Southwest and the American Northwest; its name is a ruse, so that the Coalition and heroes take it for Tolkeen rebels, while Dai waits for the great powers to wear one another down. A town with a big brewery could hold the whole army for a long while.', 'Rifts World Book 35: Megaverse in Flames p.162-163'),
('spike-the-hangdog-daemonix', 'Spike the Hangdog Daemonix', 'Gerlac Bal (true name)', 'Overlord Dai''s mount, companion, adviser and lieutenant', 'rifts', 'Hangdog Daemonix', 'None; experience level not applicable (as printed)', NULL, 'Aberrant', '600 years old, but could be immortal', '11 feet (3.4 m) at the shoulder, 19 feet (5.8 m) long', '15 tons', '{"IQ":6,"ME":7,"MA":2,"PS":42,"PP":18,"PE":23,"PB":1,"Spd":58}', 283, 190, 460, 199, 14, 14, 14, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":1,"strike":6,"parry":3,"dodge":4,"pull":2,"roll":4}', 'Spd 58 (40 mph/64 km). Hit Points 283, S.D.C. 190 and A.R. 14 are the block''s S.D.C.-setting figures. Horror Factor 15 when he charges in with Dai riding on his back. Also +4 to save vs Horror Factor and +4 vs magic. Supernatural P.S. 42.', '[{"name":"Camouflage","pct":70},{"name":"Climbing","pct":80},{"name":"Detect Ambush","pct":70},{"name":"Detect Concealment","pct":50},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":95},{"name":"Mathematics: Basic","pct":70},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":98}]', 'Skills of note only. Climbing is printed 80%/20% and the first figure is kept.', 'Fast, and able to run and labour for days on end without tiring. Swims 70%, holds his breath for 30 minutes and survives depths as great as one mile (1.6 km). Tracks by scent 50%, or 70% on blood or decay. Digs and excavates. Nightvision 1 mile (1.6 km). Heals 3D6+10 M.D.C. every 24 hours. Speaks and understands every language by magic at 90%, though he is illiterate. Cold and disease, magical forms included, cannot harm him; fire and heat do him half damage. Superhuman cargo capacity: he can pull P.S. x 1,000 pounds, 42,000 pounds (21 tons). Vulnerabilities: those of every Hangdog Daemonix; drunk or apart from Dai he is easily swayed and tricked, though he is at Dai''s side 90% of the time.', 'None.', 'Deaden Senses (4) and Ectoplasm (6 or 12). I.S.P. 14; a Minor Psychic.', NULL, NULL, 'Still wears the Tolkeen battle platform, with seats for two on his back, mounting a pair of Star Fire Cannons and a rear-firing Techno-Wizard telekinetic cannon. Each cannon fires 10 times, after which every further shot draws 25 P.P.E. from Spike himself, which is when Dai stops firing.', 'None, but Dai treats him like a king.', 'Grouchy and quarrelsome except around Dai, with whom he is unexpectedly playful. A cheerful drunk who tends to doze off once he has had his fill.', 'Overlord Dai above all, whom he would die to protect; through Dai he now commands other Daemonix, Deevils and henchmen.', 'Those of Overlord Dai and the Tolkeen Avengers.', 'Born to the station of a Daemonix that serves and is never more, Spike resented it for ages and accepted it all the same, until the day his rider died and he met Dai, which he counts as the day he was freed. The Imp treats him as an equal, asks his opinion and follows his advice, though it seldom deserves following, and lets him boss around the other Daemonix, Deevils and hirelings, which he adores. He wants nothing for himself beyond being Dai''s friend, protector and counsellor, and will fight and die to keep that place. He carries Dai into battle wearing a gun platform left over from the Tolkeen war.', 'Rifts World Book 35: Megaverse in Flames p.163-164');
